Note: `AGameModeBase::HandleStartingNewPlayer` is `BlueprintNativeEvent`, so the C++ override uses the `_Implementation` suffix.

2. **Implement in `WjWorldGameModePlay.cpp`:**
```cpp
void AWjWorldGameModePlay::HandleStartingNewPlayer_Implementation(APlayerController* NewPlayer)
{
    if (!NewPlayer) return;

    // Check if this is a mid-game joiner
    AWjWorldGameStatePlay* GS = GetGameState<AWjWorldGameStatePlay>();
    if (GS)
    {
        EGamePhase Phase = GS->GetGamePhase();
        if (Phase == EGamePhase::Playing || Phase == EGamePhase::Finished)
        {
            // Mid-game joiner: DO NOT spawn pawn (spectator mode)
            UE_LOG(LogWjWorld, Log, TEXT("GameModePlay: Mid-game joiner %s - entering spectator mode (Phase: %d)"),
                *NewPlayer->GetName(), static_cast<int32>(Phase));

            // Set to view-only (no pawn, free camera)
            NewPlayer->ChangeState(NAME_Spectating);
            return;
        }
    }

    // Normal flow: spawn pawn
    Super::HandleStartingNewPlayer_Implementation(NewPlayer);
}
```

**Key design choice:** Using `ChangeState(NAME_Spectating)` puts the PlayerController into the built-in spectating state. `APlayerController` has built-in spectator states even with `AGameModeBase`. The `NAME_Spectating` state is a built-in name that activates free-look camera without a pawn.

**Edge case -- Ready phase:** During the Ready phase (countdown before game starts), players should still spawn normally. The check above only blocks during `Playing` and `Finished` phases. If someone joins during the Ready countdown, they get a pawn and participate normally. This is correct because the game hasn't started yet.

**Testing:** Start a game, have another player join mid-game. Verify they don't get a pawn and are in spectator camera. They should see the game world but have no character.

